# LF everywhere: the tests compare the README, the desktop entries and the
# generated docs byte for byte, and install.sh must not gain CRs. Git for
# Windows checks out CRLF by default, which failed those tests there.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.ico binary

# Windows PowerShell 5.1, the one an unprepared machine has, mis-parses
# here-strings in an LF script. The scripts carry CRLF and a UTF-8 BOM.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
